  {
   "index": 5,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 393,
   "text": "A joint account is a bank account that more than one person can use.\nIt can be any kind of bank account: savings, transaction or term deposit. The type you choose depends on who you're sharing the account with and why. For example, you might choose a savings account if you and your partner are saving for a house. Or a transaction account if you're sharing rent and groceries with housemates.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 3,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
    "repeats": 2,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
