   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 555,
   "text": "Having joint access means the other account holders can take money out of the account.\nSome accounts need one account holder's signature to use the account. Other accounts need everyone to sign. Think about which option works best for you. Are you happy for other account holders to get money from the account without your signature? Are they happy for you to do the same?\nTransaction accounts come w",
